Watch out: *Will live* and *will be living* do not show how long something will have continued up to that future point.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show how long an action will have continued up to a point in the future."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a future time (*by December*, *by the time she arrives*) together with a length of time (*for ten years*, *for three hours*)."},{"label":"Example","text":"By December, I *will have been living* here for ten years."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"*Will live* and *will be living* do not show how long something will have continued up to that future point."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-01-001-28-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Future Continuous (*will be* + *-ing*)', body = 'When to use: To describe an action that will be in progress at a particular time in the future.
Look for: a specific future time (*at 8 p.m. tonight*, *this time next week*) or a time clause (*when you arrive*).
Example: At 8 o’clock tonight, I *will be studying* for my Spanish test.
Watch out: Do not add *been* (*will have been* + *-ing*) unless the sentence tells you how long the action will have lasted (*for three hours*).', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To describe an action that will be in progress at a particular time in the future."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a specific future time (*at 8 p.m. tonight*, *this time next week*) or a time clause (*when you arrive*)."},{"label":"Example","text":"At 8 o’clock tonight, I *will be studying* for my Spanish test."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not add *been* (*will have been* + *-ing*) unless the sentence tells you how long the action will have lasted (*for three hours*)."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-01-001-29-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Future Perfect (*will have* + past participle)', body = 'When to use: To say that an action will be finished before a particular time in the future.
Look for: a future deadline (*by next week*, *by 2030*, *by the time you arrive*).
Example: By next week, I *will have completed* all the assignments.
Watch out: Use *will be* + *-ing* for an action in progress at a future time, and *will have been* + *-ing* to focus on how long an action will have lasted.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To say that an action will be finished before a particular time in the future."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a future deadline (*by next week*, *by 2030*, *by the time you arrive*)."},{"label":"Example","text":"By next week, I *will have completed* all the assignments."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Use *will be* + *-ing* for an action in progress at a future time, and *will have been* + *-ing* to focus on how long an action will have lasted."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-01-001-30-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Past Continuous (*was/were* + *-ing*)', body = 'When to use: To describe an action that was in progress at a particular moment in the past, often when something else happened.
Look for: *at 9 p.m. last night*, *at that moment*, *while…*, *when the phone rang*.
Example: I *was studying* for the test when the power went out.
Watch out: Use *had been* + *-ing* only when the sentence tells you how long the action had continued (*for three hours*).', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To describe an action that was in progress at a particular moment in the past, often when something else happened."},{"label":"Look for","text":"*at 9 p.m. last night*, *at that moment*, *while…*, *when the phone rang*."},{"label":"Example","text":"I *was studying* for the test when the power went out."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Use *had been* + *-ing* only when the sentence tells you how long the action had continued (*for three hours*)."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-01-002-01-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Past Perfect (*had* + past participle)', body = 'When to use: To show that one past action happened before another past action or time.
Look for: *by 10 p.m.*, *before she called*, *by the time the meeting started*, *already*.
Example: By the time the meeting started, I *had finished* the report.
Watch out: If events are told in the order they happened, the simple past is usually enough (*I finished the report and went home*). Use *had* + past participle when you need to show which action happened first.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show that one past action happened before another past action or time."},{"label":"Look for","text":"*by 10 p.m.*, *before she called*, *by the time the meeting started*, *already*."},{"label":"Example","text":"By the time the meeting started, I *had finished* the report."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"If events are told in the order they happened, the simple past is usually enough (*I finished the report and went home*). Use *had* + past participle when you need to show which action happened first."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-01-002-02-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Past Perfect Continuous (*had been* + *-ing*)', body = 'When to use: To show how long an action had continued up to a point in the past.
