Look for: evidence such as *Look at those clouds!* or *Watch out!*, or a plan already made (*I’ve decided to…*).
Example: Look at those dark clouds. It *is going to rain*.
Watch out: When there is clear evidence right now, *be going to* is more natural than *will*: *Be careful – he’s going to fall!*', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"For plans or intentions decided before speaking, and for predictions based on what you can see now."},{"label":"Look for","text":"evidence such as *Look at those clouds!* or *Watch out!*, or a plan already made (*I’ve decided to…*)."},{"label":"Example","text":"Look at those dark clouds. It *is going to rain*."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"When there is clear evidence right now, *be going to* is more natural than *will*: *Be careful – he’s going to fall!*"}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-01-004-19-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Present Continuous for arrangements', body = 'When to use: For personal plans that have already been arranged, usually with a fixed time, place or other people.
Look for: verbs such as *meet*, *visit*, *fly*, *stay* and *have dinner*, with a future time (*this Friday*, *next weekend*).
Example: I *am meeting* the academic committee this Friday.
Watch out: The simple present is mainly used for public timetables. For your own arrangements, *I’m flying to London tomorrow* is more natural than *I fly to London tomorrow*.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"For personal plans that have already been arranged, usually with a fixed time, place or other people."},{"label":"Look for","text":"verbs such as *meet*, *visit*, *fly*, *stay* and *have dinner*, with a future time (*this Friday*, *next weekend*)."},{"label":"Example","text":"I *am meeting* the academic committee this Friday."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"The simple present is mainly used for public timetables. For your own arrangements, *I’m flying to London tomorrow* is more natural than *I fly to London tomorrow*."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-01-004-20-00';
