UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Looking back at the past (*should have*, *ought to have*, *could have*, *would have* + past participle)', body = 'When to use: To talk about past actions that did not happen: regrets, criticism, missed chances and imagined results.
Key difference: *should have* / *ought to have* = it was the right thing to do, but it did not happen (*shouldn’t have* = it was wrong, but it happened); *could have* = it was possible, but it did not happen; *would have* = the imagined result if things had been different.
Look for: regret or criticism (*It was a mistake…*, *Unfortunately…*, *In hindsight…*) or a missed chance (*…but we chose…*).
Examples: You *should have checked* the date before paying. We *could have taken* the express train, but we chose the bus.
Watch out: *Should have* is about what was right to do; *could have* is about what was possible to do.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To talk about past actions that did not happen: regrets, criticism, missed chances and imagined results."},{"label":"Key difference","text":"*should have* / *ought to have* = it was the right thing to do, but it did not happen (*shouldn’t have* = it was wrong, but it happened); *could have* = it was possible, but it did not happen; *would have* = the imagined result if things had been different."},{"label":"Look for","text":"regret or criticism (*It was a mistake…*, *Unfortunately…*, *In hindsight…*) or a missed chance (*…but we chose…*)."},{"label":"Examples","text":"You *should have checked* the date before paying. We *could have taken* the express train, but we chose the bus."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"*Should have* is about what was right to do; *could have* is about what was possible to do."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-02-010-01-00';
