UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Talking about part of a group (*some of which*, *most of whom*)', body = 'When to use: To say how many or how much of a group you have just mentioned.
Key difference: *of whom* = people (*two of whom*, *all of whom*); *of which* = things (*some of which*, *none of which*).
Look for: a plural group earlier in the sentence, followed by a comma and a word such as *all*, *most*, *some*, *none* or a number.
Examples: She invited twenty guests, *most of whom* arrived on time. I ordered four parcels, *two of which* have already arrived.
