Watch out: Use *Having done*, not *Had done* or the base verb: *Having reviewed the notes, he felt ready*, not *Had reviewed the notes, he felt ready*.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show that one action was completed before the next one."},{"label":"Look for","text":"two actions in sequence by the same person."},{"label":"Example","text":"*Having finished* her homework, she went out to play."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Use *Having done*, not *Had done* or the base verb: *Having reviewed the notes, he felt ready*, not *Had reviewed the notes, he felt ready*."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-05-025-17-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Adding information (*moreover*, *furthermore*, *in addition*)', body = 'When to use: To add another point that supports what you have just said.
Look for: a second sentence that adds a similar or stronger point.
Example: The hotel was cheap. *Moreover*, it was close to the beach.
Watch out: Do not join two sentences with only a comma: *It was cheap. Moreover, it was close to the beach*, not *It was cheap, moreover it was close to the beach*.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To add another point that supports what you have just said."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a second sentence that adds a similar or stronger point."},{"label":"Example","text":"The hotel was cheap. *Moreover*, it was close to the beach."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not join two sentences with only a comma: *It was cheap. Moreover, it was close to the beach*, not *It was cheap, moreover it was close to the beach*."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-05-025-18-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Results (*therefore*, *consequently*, *as a result*, *otherwise*)', body = 'When to use: To show that one thing is the result of another.
Key difference: *therefore* / *consequently* / *as a result* = so; *otherwise* = if not.
Example: Hurry up; *otherwise*, we will miss the bus.
Watch out: Use *otherwise* for ‘if not’, not *therefore*: *Leave now; otherwise you''ll be late*.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show that one thing is the result of another."},{"label":"Key difference","text":"*therefore* / *consequently* / *as a result* = so; *otherwise* = if not."},{"label":"Example","text":"Hurry up; *otherwise*, we will miss the bus."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Use *otherwise* for ‘if not’, not *therefore*: *Leave now; otherwise you''ll be late*."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-05-025-19-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Short time phrases (*while* / *after* / *before* / *upon* + *-ing*)', body = 'When to use: To shorten a time clause when both parts have the same subject (*While I was waiting* → *While waiting*).
Look for: *while*, *after*, *before*, *on* or *upon* followed by an *-ing* form.
Example: *Upon arriving* at the hotel, we checked in immediately.
Watch out: The person after the comma must be the one doing the action: *While waiting for the bus, I saw a friend*, not *While waiting for the bus, a friend saw me*.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To shorten a time clause when both parts have the same subject (*While I was waiting* → *While waiting*)."},{"label":"Look for","text":"*while*, *after*, *before*, *on* or *upon* followed by an *-ing* form."},{"label":"Example","text":"*Upon arriving* at the hotel, we checked in immediately."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"The person after the comma must be the one doing the action: *While waiting for the bus, I saw a friend*, not *While waiting for the bus, a friend saw me*."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-05-025-20-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Contrast (*however*, *nevertheless*, *in contrast*, *on the other hand*)', body = 'When to use: To show a contrast or an unexpected result between two sentences.
Key difference: *however* / *nevertheless* = an unexpected result; *in contrast* / *on the other hand* = a comparison of two things.
Example: The test was difficult. *Nevertheless*, most students passed.
Watch out: *however* links sentences, not clauses: *It was late. However, we stayed*, not *It was late however we stayed*.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show a contrast or an unexpected result between two sentences."},{"label":"Key difference","text":"*however* / *nevertheless* = an unexpected result; *in contrast* / *on the other hand* = a comparison of two things."},{"label":"Example","text":"The test was difficult. *Nevertheless*, most students passed."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"*however* links sentences, not clauses: *It was late. However, we stayed*, not *It was late however we stayed*."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-05-025-21-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = '*instead* vs *instead of*', body = 'When to use: To show that one thing replaces another.
Key difference: *instead of* + noun / *-ing* (*instead of driving*); *instead* stands alone, usually at the end or start of a clause.
Example: We didn''t drive. We took the train *instead*.
Watch out: *instead of taking the bus*, not *instead taking the bus*.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show that one thing replaces another."},{"label":"Key difference","text":"*instead of* + noun / *-ing* (*instead of driving*); *instead* stands alone, usually at the end or start of a clause."},{"label":"Example","text":"We didn''t drive. We took the train *instead*."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"*instead of taking the bus*, not *instead taking the bus*."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-05-025-22-00';
