Example: The teacher said that water *boils* at 100°C.
Watch out: You may keep the present for facts that are always true: *He said that the earth revolves around the sun*.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"When the reported words are a scientific fact, a general truth or something still true."},{"label":"Look for","text":"facts about nature, science or permanent habits."},{"label":"Example","text":"The teacher said that water *boils* at 100°C."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"You may keep the present for facts that are always true: *He said that the earth revolves around the sun*."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-07-031-21-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Reported speech: *will* → *would*', body = 'When to use: When reporting future plans, promises or predictions with a past reporting verb.
Look for: *will* or *will have* in the original words. Change to *would* / *would have*.
Example: ‘I will send the email.’ → She said she *would send* the email.
Watch out: Do not keep *will* after *said*: *She said she would call*, not *She said she will call*.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"When reporting future plans, promises or predictions with a past reporting verb."},{"label":"Look for","text":"*will* or *will have* in the original words. Change to *would* / *would have*."},{"label":"Example","text":"‘I will send the email.’ → She said she *would send* the email."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not keep *will* after *said*: *She said she would call*, not *She said she will call*."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-07-031-22-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = 'Reported speech: past → past perfect', body = 'When to use: When the original words were already in the past and you report them later.
Look for: a past event inside the reported words. *did* → *had done*; *was doing* → *had been doing*.
Example: ‘I lost my keys.’ → She said she *had lost* her keys.
Watch out: Use *had* + past participle to show the event happened earlier: *had lost*, not *has lost*.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"When the original words were already in the past and you report them later."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a past event inside the reported words. *did* → *had done*; *was doing* → *had been doing*."},{"label":"Example","text":"‘I lost my keys.’ → She said she *had lost* her keys."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Use *had* + past participle to show the event happened earlier: *had lost*, not *has lost*."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-07-031-23-00';
