Watch out: Use *-ing* after the linking word: *While waiting*, not *While wait* or *While waited*.', fields_json = '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To shorten a clause when both parts have the same subject (*While I was waiting* → *While waiting*)."},{"label":"Look for","text":"one of these words with no subject after it, then an *-ing* form."},{"label":"Example","text":"*While waiting* for the bus, she read a book."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Use *-ing* after the linking word: *While waiting*, not *While wait* or *While waited*."}]' WHERE feedback_code = '01-01-11-055-01-00';
UPDATE feedback_items SET heading = '*When* / *Once* / *Unless* / *Although* + past participle', body = 'When to use: To shorten a clause with a passive meaning (*Once they are washed* → *Once washed*).
Look for: one of these words with no subject after it, where the subject receives the action.
Example: *Once washed*, the vegetables are ready to cook.
